# Middleware Folder
# 
# Purpose: Reusable functions that process requests before they reach route handlers
# 
# Best Practices:
# - Create reusable middleware functions for common tasks
# - One middleware per concern (authentication, validation, logging, error handling)
# - Middleware should be composable and chainable
# - Use TypeScript for type safety in middleware
# - Handle errors in dedicated error handling middleware
# - Keep middleware focused on a single responsibility
# - Export middleware functions for easy importing
# - Test middleware independently
# 
# Example middleware:
# - errorHandler.ts (global error handling)
# - validation.ts (request validation)
# - auth.ts (authentication/authorization)
# - logger.ts (request logging)
# - rateLimiter.ts (rate limiting)

